    "created_at": "2022-05-27T20:47:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-27T20:49:05Z",
    "body": "The tag omission sections are meant to be summaries for authors, and in particular only apply to conforming documents. So they don't mention non-conforming elements such as bgsound or basefont, and they don't apply to cases like the ones you list with a lone body end tag.\r\n\r\nSee also the definition of that section: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-tag-omission\r\n\r\nI'll close this since it seems to be conflating the non-normative summaries (what you're quoting) with the normative parser spec. But happy to discuss further in the closed thread.\r\n\r\nIn particular, try to run any \"inputs\" through https://validator.w3.org/ to check that they're conforming, which is the only time this advice applies.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
