    "body": "@domenic thank you for aswer, will be great to add this to docs:\r\n\r\n> The tag omission sections are meant to be summaries for authors, and in particular only apply to conforming documents. So they don't mention non-conforming elements such as bgsound or basefont, and they don't apply to cases like the ones you list with a lone body end tag.\r\n\r\nBecause is not clarify that:\r\n\r\n> A non-normative description of whether, in the [text/html](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#text/html) syntax, the [start](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-start-tag) and [end](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-end-tag) tags can be omitted. This information is redundant with the normative requirements given in the [optional tags](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-tag-omission) section, and is provided in the element definitions only as a convenience.\r\n\r\n\r\nI implemented tag omission in serializer for HTML minification, so I used these rules to omit tags where it is possible, but looks there are more cases especial for adoption logic and reconstruction active elements.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
