    "body": "@domenic Oh, yes, my mistake, sorry.\r\n\r\n> i.e. not something you should ever use to implement anything.\r\n\r\nThis is rather strange because if parser handles these cases we can compress valid HTML file and avoid extra tags and so we will have less HTML size, but yes, I provided cases where we have errors and non-conforming examples.\r\n\r\nSo shorty - it is safe for any valid HTML document(i.e. conforming), right?\r\n\r\nI will check all my cases, if I will found something I will return here with example.\r\n\r\nAnd thank you again for fast answer",
